# Nothing unversioned reaches the build context (review finding G-026).
#
# Docker sends the whole context directory to the daemon before the Dockerfile
# is even read. Files the Dockerfile never COPYs still travel, land in the
# build cache and can end up in an intermediate layer. A .dockerignore is the
# only place that stops it.
#
# Same reasoning as the deploy manifest (G-020): what the project treats as a
# secret is gitignored, so the rule here mirrors .gitignore rather than
# inventing a second list to keep in sync.

secrets/
*.env
!*.env.example
*token*
!test_*token*
*.key
*.pem
# Names without an extension slip through the patterns above - the agent's
# anthropic_api_key was the one this test actually caught.
*api_key*
*secret*
*credential*

# Local state and test residue - never wanted in an image, and a state file
# can carry message ids and reply ids.
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Evidence, manifests and archives: large, and none of it belongs in a build.
DEPLOY_MANIFEST.txt
*.bundle
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.zip
.DS_Store
._*
